}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+\\frac{5}{2}+(-2)=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259629 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6347f5f0-9e16-5206-aff9-2c2763ded762" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257657} {:answer/id #uuid "945359d7-fb4c-5dc5-b2a6-bb81fdb84705" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258090} {:answer/id #uuid "c91b887a-085e-55d3-a82d-f0f2a9ebbd18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258534} {:answer/id #uuid "cb0c3b3c-a63e-56f7-adf1-6c30a48415eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258544} {:answer/id #uuid "df8ff073-69ba-50cc-bc91-0935eff1238a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257657} :answer-field/id #uuid "32802996-0705-5f7c-88e9-ff4e636541d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259124}] :question/id #uuid "e5caf03b-dafd-5e12-a099-434c9d099a24" :question/math-academy-id "q-124235" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind $a+b+c,$ given that the matrix form of the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ a & b\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix form of $T$ gives us the following information:\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-2\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot 4}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+\\frac{3}{2}+(-\\frac{5}{2})=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259632 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09e100c0-d6ff-5136-87d3-6d7c4cb5f7a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256869} {:answer/id #uuid "4115a4dc-a26c-5fa3-9586-57c831ab287a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257360} {:answer/id #uuid "777f54f7-5bed-5e04-a701-aa0d0d8361f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257840} {:answer/id #uuid "907c2819-9860-5a07-9077-f754b8f1532c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258051} {:answer/id #uuid "aa493f4d-9eda-598d-987d-713420f94752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256869} :answer-field/id #uuid "d89e1981-b198-5567-8250-810bdc62696a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259413}] :question/id #uuid "d10dbe8c-a132-5e08-bb9b-f3f11298186b" :question/math-academy-id "q-124238" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind $a+b+c,$ given that the matrix form of the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a & -3 \\\\ 1 & b\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix form of $T$ gives us the following information:\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot (-5)-(-9)\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-2+\\frac{5}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}=0.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259633 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/ch