d}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dad9073-478b-54b1-a7af-14e9b549d134" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 \\\\ 14 & 10 \\\\ -15 & -35\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533174} {:answer/id #uuid "0f783940-c57e-5b76-b2a2-204a0ec5ec07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 14 \\\\ 10 & -15 & -35\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533178} {:answer/id #uuid "9d1db3e7-b40d-5dd2-8056-ba5fbb14c5dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 & 30 \\\\ 18 & 45 \\\\ 42 & 105\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533520} {:answer/id #uuid "a46cedc9-7f50-57d8-8219-01fc7f258e44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533537} {:answer/id #uuid "cdb01e9d-e482-500b-8961-81b00c565787" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 18 & 42 \\\\ 30 & -45 & -105\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 18 & 42 \\\\ 30 & -45 & -105\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533637} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6ef3817-fd8a-50ea-a054-edd21587414d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533962}] :question/id #uuid "55449077-495e-5404-a705-ef8294705226" :question/math-academy-id "q-269371" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 3}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=3({y}^{T}Ax)$ where \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1\\en