ed}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=2([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}])=2([\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 14 & -7 & 0\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 28 & -14 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549991 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5431fd3a-c958-5840-b6fc-bd80d1d983c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549487} {:answer/id #uuid "ab469b17-e684-57f3-a032-921d53d60e0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549637} {:answer/id #uuid "d75faa5d-b436-5bf2-80c6-7dd3b873f64d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549715} {:answer/id #uuid "f3189ab9-689f-5420-a82c-7c912aa81e2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549770} {:answer/id #uuid "fc7ffc60-8c50-5d64-a8a1-dfe85be3ab2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549637} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d683c36-c6df-5d48-954b-faab60c2b7e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549847}] :question/id #uuid "b06d01a6-0f9f-5c10-83f5-9d9f497a0fba" :question/math-academy-id "q-269387" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{3\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)={y}^{T}Ax$ where \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWriting out $L$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\nL={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{a}_{ij}{y}_{i}{x}_{j},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${∇}_{A}L=y\\cdot {x}^{T}.$\n\nEvaluating at the given values $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Gradient of a Function Component-Wise"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204081 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203866 :question/id #uuid "429a6a34-2fe5-5c09-9b74-e4b650209007" :question/math-academy-id "e-17870" :question/problem "Consider the function $L: \\mathbb{R}^{2 \\times 3}   \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ defined by $L(\\mathbf{A}) = \\dfrac{1}{2}(\\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{b})^T(\\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{b}),$ where\n![](images/51/518bfea30c779d3e9dc1ab6b77b0ddaa9b938b56b0bb3b9e68d6c9b9cdae5666.svg)\nWhat is $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{A}} L$ at \n![](images/a1/a1e2b39a295cebfd8425e8ab73e4d915233ca3afbd4141c54332c38f1091be15.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $\\mathbf{A}$ is a matrix of the same shape as $\\mathbf{A}$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial L}{\\partial a_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $\\mathbf{A}.$\n\nWe can compute $\\dfrac{\\partial L}{\\partial a_{ij}}$ by applying the chain rule.\n\nLet $\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{b} \\in \\mathbb{R}^2.$ Then, $L(\\mathbf{A}) = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{y}^T\\mathbf{y}$ and\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial L}{\\partial a_{ij}} = \\sum_{k=1}^2 \\dfrac{\\partial L}{\\partial y_k} \\cdot \\dfrac{\\partial y_k}{\\partial a_{ij}}\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf{y}} L = \\nabla_{\\mathbf{y}} \\bigg( \\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{y}^T\\mathbf{y} \\bigg) = \\mathbf{y},\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial L}{\\partial y_k} = y_k.\n$$\n\nWriting out $\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{b}$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\ny_i = \\sum\\limits_{j=1}^3 (a_{ij} x_j - b_i),\n$$\n\nwe have \n\n- $\\dfrac{\\partial y_k}{\\partial a_{ij}} = x_j$ if $i = k$, and\n\n- $\\dfrac{\\partial y_k}{\\partial a_{ij}} = 0$ if $i \\neq k.$\n\nThis means that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}} & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{i}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & ={y}_{i}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & ={y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $(i,j)$th entry of $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{A}} L$ is the $i$th entry of $\\mathbf{y}$ multiplied by the $j$th entry of $\\mathbf{x}$, so\n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf{A}} L = \\mathbf{y} \\cdot \\mathbf{x}^T.\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{A}} L$ at ![](images/ee/ee9b9f891c92caf4229e8e92c20031fe7ba9e1cc0472105caf5a6cfaa8541a27.svg) we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{A}L & =y\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =(Ax-b)\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =([\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef7b2139-06eb-5584-a267-d9fbc9b5d041" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204583 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "390d31e7-0eb4-5afa-8052-7ccdd44c6579" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549433} :answer-field/id #uuid "a792c03a-20d1-502a-87d8-51c51290a0f7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203428} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bf55f8d-69c2-5804-b198-4e612f8ef966" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "260" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "260" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549469} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8fb804b-e34c-5518-b27d-f7e1b108969b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203429} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d24effe3-93a6-51e3-92fb-67753603fb63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549705} :answer-field/id #uuid "f24f27c1-d129-569d-91c5-ec978eca7083" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203430} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1be0ef3-af8e-50ef-8a85-884fab6e57c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "130" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "130" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549731} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b648609-00c6-5d8f-b7a0-5619dddfcab1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203431}] :question/id #uuid "c38068fb-d53f-5bd3-995e-1c6838e1f711" :question/math-academy-id "q-269257" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 3}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=\\frac{1}{2}(Ax-b)^{T}(Ax-b),$ where\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${∇}_{A}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-160$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWe can compute $\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}$ by applying the chain rule.\n\nLet $y=Ax-b\\in {R}^{2}.$ Then, $L(A)=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{T}y$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n{∇}_{y}L={∇}_{y}(\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{T}y)=y,\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}={y}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWriting out $y=Ax-b$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\n{y}_{i}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}{a}_{ij}{x}_{j}-{b}_{i},\n$$\n\nwe have \n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}={x}_{j}$ if $i=k$, and\n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}=0$ if $i\\ne k.$\n\nThis means that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}} & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{i}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & ={y}_{i}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & ={y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $(i,j)$th entry of ${∇}_{A}L$ is the $i$th entry of $y$ multiplied by the $j$th entry of $x$, so\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=y\\cdot {x}^{T}.\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating ${∇}_{A}L$ at $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{A}L & =y\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =(Ax-b)\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =([\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 10 & 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =([\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 10 & 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 10 & 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 130 & 260 \\\\ 0 & -80 & -160\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204585 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff0f6ad8-5133-5024-a578-c55897acba97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "528" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "528" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533766} :answer-field/id #uuid "95ff86ad-4fd6-5245-9c4f-f316fd454074" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203438} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ef11ea8-6ba0-5016-814e-da90180fe8bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 