\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n{∇}_{y}L={∇}_{y}({y}^{T}y)=2y,\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}=2{y}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWriting out $y=4Ax-5b$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\n{y}_{i}=4{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{a}_{ij}{x}_{j}-5{b}_{i},\n$$\n\nwe have \n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}=4{x}_{j}$ if $i=k$, and\n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}=0$ if $i\\ne k.$\n\nThis means that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}} & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{i}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =2{y}_{i}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =2{y}_{i}\\cdot 4{x}_{j} \\\\  & =8{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $(i,j)$th entry of ${∇}_{A}L$ is $8$ times the $i$th entry of $y$ multiplied by the $j$th entry of $x$, so\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=8y\\cdot {x}^{T}.\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating ${∇}_{A}L$ at $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{A}L & =8y\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =8(4Ax-5b)\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =8(4[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-5[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =8([\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -16\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}208 \\\\ -248\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 832 \\\\ 0 & -992\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542179 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e1e29d1-1888-52aa-8dc6-4b2845f73611" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541611} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fa668de-a737-5f91-800a-6c4b031f88c5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542015} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33107365-8d72-59e7-84e4-fb7248465cbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541529} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd131918-eda5-51aa-9124-e861cbcfd218" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542109}] :question/id #uuid "a276eb8e-dc20-5069-8231-5e2d2d2a281a" :question/math-academy-id "q-269429" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=\\frac{1}{2}(Ax-b)^{T}(Ax-b),$ where\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${∇}_{A}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWe can compute $\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}$ by applying the chain rule.\n\nLet $y=Ax-b\\in {R}^{2}.$ Then, $L(A)=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{T}y$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n{∇}_{y}L={∇}_{y}(\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{T}y)=y,\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}={y}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWriting out $y=Ax-b$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\n{y}_{i}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{a}_{ij}{x}_{j}-{b}_{i},\n$$\n\nwe have \n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}={x}_{j}$ if $i=k$, and\n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}=0$ if $i\\ne k.$\n\nThis means that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}} & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{i}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & ={y}_{i}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & ={y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $(i,j)$th entry of ${∇}_{A}L$ is the $i$th entry of $y$ multiplied by the $j$th entry of $x$, so\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=y\\cdot {x}^{T}.\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating ${∇}_{A}L$ at $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{A}L & =y\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =(Ax-b)\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 \\\\ -6 & -9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549924 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4d4fb6a-d27b-55cc-8727-67a4c04b568b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "760" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "760" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549652} :answer-field/id #uuid "86a09f03-3f8a-5c3f-9183-dbfb9af6dd2a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549863} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eeb1139b-d9f2-55ff-8169-1877c0fc480b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549755} :answer-field/id #uuid "a107a0f3-3d37-50c0-a77a-33925b86f16a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549878}] :question/id #uuid "078844cb-65ac-54f4-bde7-64e4bd44f313" :question/math-academy-id "q-269466" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=2(Ax-b)^{T}(Ax-b),$ where\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${∇}_{A}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$760$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-40$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWe can compute $\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}$ by applying the chain rule.\n\nLet $y=Ax-b\\in {R}^{2}.$ Then, $L(A)=2{y}^{T}y$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n{∇}_{y}L={∇}_{y}(2{y}^{T}y)=4y,\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}=4{y}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWriting out $y=Ax-b$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\n{y}_{i}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{a}_{ij}{x}_{j}-{b}_{i}.\n$$\n\nwe have \n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}={x}_{j}$ if $i=k$, and\n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}=0$ if $i\\ne k.$\n\nThis means that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}} & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{i}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =4{y}_{i}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =4{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $(i,j)$th entry of ${∇}_{A}L$ is $4$ times the $i$th entry of $y$ multiplied by the $j$th entry of $x,$ so\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=4y\\cdot {x}^{T}.\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating ${∇}_{A}L$ at $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{A}L & =4y\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =4(Ax-b)\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =4([\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 & 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4([\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 & 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}76 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 & 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}760 & 760 \\\\ -40 & -40\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Chain Rule to Calculate Gradients"}] :topic/math-academy-id 5869 :topic/title "Matrix Gradients"}]}
